<title>ITALY: Italy set to seek ERM lira re-entry end-Nov-Ciampi.</title>
<headline>Italy set to seek ERM lira re-entry end-Nov-Ciampi.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said on Wednesday that Italy was likely to seek a re-entry of the lira into the Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) at the end of the month.</p>
<p>&quot;Italy will probably ask for the lira's re-entry into the ERM during a weekend at the end of November,&quot; Ciampi told a news conference.  </p>
<p>Italy has repeatedly said it would seek to return the lira to the currency grid after the 1997 budget is approved by the Chamber of Deputies (lower house), expected late next week.</p>
<p>The lira crashed out of the ERM in September 1992 amid currency turmoil.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
